{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Online TLS certificate rotation on self-managed mongod and mongos",
  "slug": "online-tls-certificate-rotation-on-self-managed-mongod-and-mongos",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:4ec6b801463272815182005d751dbfb25408fd453e4b2f5ce6fc9724fe1694de",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "1f2974e5d2b64f4bfe19e125908bf591bc7ba5a1de9c21df5f6f59f0caedcd61",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:381f9dc912624a4aff9372313bfd45597ef1245858ae4db5829b8f5874323bb6",
      "text": "Validate certificate details and trust before deployment, retain previous files for rollback, and test a fresh connection after replacement. An established session alone does not demonstrate successful use of renewed material. Inspect rotation logs as part of validation. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/",
        "https://docs.itential.com/itential-platform/administer/mongodb"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:155eb55877da47fa6d5824ce07e954c0e74bb978266d8e0915be53be33669ef9",
        "ev:6e9670fbb0327d21a5aeabecc173bcb89df69429a4d7f23a6fb4eb4ddc6c2aa5",
        "ev:bc578b93bed0cd4d5562daf163c5148d66252891f59d1bf64ec3b74ce68ff458"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1bd2d486597334e6fcdd4fb049b2529cf84297f97d5753ff35ed074a16085d68",
      "text": "For MongoDB 8.0, replace configured PEM files, then run db.adminCommand({rotateCertificates: 1}) against each target mongod or mongos. The command was introduced in 5.0; db.rotateCertificates() wraps it. Rotation is process-local and can run regardless of replication status. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/",
        "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-net-tls-secure-connections/view",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:a900bdf646ff975ec35fc16587f84c7a292aae48e9fc2bf89ba0c06d5b290309",
        "ev:af40448a02567d7a017f1a0c8f35ef793c014dca90a954f75d8164a8fd5daf23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e9c52a1f7cba521d2f1e29bf0a0a5261d0b18e578f2d6132104aa4fd887dcf11",
      "text": "Incorrect, expired, revoked or missing certificate files cause rotation to fail without invalidating the loaded TLS configuration or terminating mongod or mongos. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md",
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0263723f3a2711d606eaa7fbefae6dd4e138bf986951ebf55d571736d1b09268"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f63028dc36aa4bd31ba6bf5e0935771931f98518dff74c176b1d0d3497b2a99e",
      "text": "Only one rotation may run per process, regardless of replication status. A concurrent rotation errors; tlsCertificateSelector=thumbprint also fails rotation and logs a warning. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4f0ffd631cb7d0b715da2251ddf80084d256a982eea57f995f3e68d072988547",
        "ev:5da047cfcbe8e4e8efe5fa2816c4d27a7e4a2954bbb83d4e2b4ecffff19f6335"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:7b3937aed1c8ecd5dbd52c637458d917529d340379de004366ae522e0ecd2570",
      "text": "Percona's August 31, 2026 procedure explicitly covers same-CA renewal with unchanged X.509 membership attributes. It excludes changing the issuing CA or subject identity from that procedure; this restriction does not mean MongoDB cannot reload a CA file. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-08-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4dd1be1d327e06dea6f1400a8538bbd28a03a8d407576f9e70f863f90dfef6c7",
        "ev:c5f79abb7f3bda055dfaafffe6a87cca2c835a1478a892e49fb0013d79ea1ddb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d9bb38f75bdcb613a9dd440e8a381e3dfe760e3cd9e453644c58d88bed193378",
      "text": "Replacement files must retain their configured filenames and paths. Encrypted certificateKeyFile replacements must retain the configured password; interactive password prompting is unsupported. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:98a432de9b3898bc1e898b2935a6c95b8f3b01ba93c9ef4091fdffc95f766998"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6a75443f4f54c5340b2c116686f425991a197ca9e135e2624e7fcce97654d30a",
      "text": "MongoDB 8.0 supports reloading TLS certificates, CA files and CRL files; CRL rotation is documented for Linux and Windows. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/rotateCertificates.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:60f258839727edf9ed88fb47f19dccfce25cebd487aea78803b59498bf1a2321",
        "ev:c5f79abb7f3bda055dfaafffe6a87cca2c835a1478a892e49fb0013d79ea1ddb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:01742bc2716f86c865ac5ea6a61bd1aeaa1fd567b15064f2f2f41cf4cef43387",
      "text": "Successful rotation preserves established connections using their old certificates; subsequent connections use the newly loaded certificates. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/",
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/rotating-expiring-x-509-certificates-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-with-minimal-service-interruption/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:bc578b93bed0cd4d5562daf163c5148d66252891f59d1bf64ec3b74ce68ff458"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0784b6a02bb1c7c57b1e3a817aff5fe66ea75175f3475a63bbb3095085554aba",
      "text": "The rotateCertificates privilege is required and is included in hostManager. Successful rotation logs certificate identity, thumbprint and validity information; enabled auditing also records it. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/method/db.rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:af5f991cee04c236297ec239ddd07fa82fd70b7b86888db6a6f6f75ffc8b3e8b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fcb6a21c9fe46856f7a146bee8366e636bfe26baacf5e67d7fe9ba080fc02dae",
      "text": "Itential's MongoDB administration procedure replaces server and CA files and uses secondary-first rolling restarts with primary stepdown. That application-specific procedure does not establish that MongoDB 8.0 requires restarts for an eligible online reload. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-31)",
      "source_url": "https://docs.itential.com/itential-platform/administer/mongodb",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.0/reference/command/rotateCertificates/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:098f505ce651dd93a1b792f20c2703eccb229f7fa5a7101cb4318bf98dc18633",
        "ev:79202e708d7680a8df7ff817b59cae4ae48b1f04e2433930301d1098adabc0e1",
        "ev:b021279b9e4e6fc96b66029a9f911b363b4819bd22ba1a54c8250287ce2e7785"
      ]
    }
  ],
